window.QUESTIONS_2024A=[{"id":1,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the combination of terms or phrases to be inserted into blanks A through C in the description below concerning a method for representing information?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"analogdigitalanalog"},{"key":"B","text":"analogdigitaldigital"},{"key":"C","text":"digitalanaloganalog"},{"key":"D","text":"digitalanalogdigital"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the combination of terms or phrases to be inserted into blanks A through C in the description below concerning a method for representing information?” The correct answer is B) analogdigitaldigital because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) analogdigitalanalog C) digitalanaloganalog D) digitalanalogdigital and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":2,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Japanese restaurants in Sapporo and Japanese restaurants in Hakodate are to be searched for together. Which of the following is the logical expression that represents the search condition?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(“Sapporo” AND “Hakodate”) AND “Japanese restaurant”"},{"key":"B","text":"(“Sapporo” AND “Hakodate”) OR “Japanese restaurant”"},{"key":"C","text":"(“Sapporo” OR “Hakodate”) AND “Japanese restaurant”"},{"key":"D","text":"(“Sapporo” OR “Hakodate”) OR “Japanese restaurant”"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Japanese restaurants in Sapporo and Japanese restaurants in Hakodate are to be searched for together. Which of the following is the logical expression that represents the search condition?” The correct answer is C) (“Sapporo” OR “Hakodate”) AND “Japanese restaurant” because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) (“Sapporo” AND “Hakodate”) AND “Japanese restaurant” B) (“Sapporo” AND “Hakodate”) OR “Japanese restaurant” D) (“Sapporo” OR “Hakodate”) OR “Japanese restaurant” and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":3,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"As shown in the figure below, decimal numbers 2, 5, 10, and 21 are represented using five (5) squares that are black or white.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"20"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"30"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “As shown in the figure below, decimal numbers 2, 5, 10, and 21 are represented using five (5) squares that are black or white.” The correct answer is C) 24 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 12 B) 20 D) 30 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":4,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When a path goes from node A1 to node C2 in Fig. 1 and the passing nodes are counted as shown in Fig. 2, there are three shortest paths with the minimum number of passing nodes. How many shortest paths are there available to go from node A1 to node D4 via node C2?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"20"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When a path goes from node A1 to node C2 in Fig. 1 and the passing nodes are counted as shown in Fig. 2, there are three shortest paths with the minimum number of passing nodes. How many shortest paths are there available to go from node A1 to node D4 via node C2?” The correct answer is B) 9 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 6 C) 12 D) 20 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":5,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning machine language?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A program that is written in Fortran or C is converted into machine language and then executed."},{"key":"B","text":"Machine language is a high-level language."},{"key":"C","text":"Machine language expresses a program with sequences of decimal numbers."},{"key":"D","text":"Most of application software is still programmed in machine language."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning machine language?” The correct answer is A) A program that is written in Fortran or C is converted into machine language and then executed. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Machine language is a high-level language. C) Machine language expresses a program with sequences of decimal numbers. D) Most of application software is still programmed in machine language. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":6,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A power company charges electricity bill shown in the table below.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(units - 100) × 5100 × 5 +(units - 100) × 10 +(units - 200) × 15"},{"key":"B","text":"(units - 100) × 5100 × 5 +200 × 10 +(units - 300) × 15"},{"key":"C","text":"units × 5100 × 5 +(units - 100) × 10 +(units - 200) × 15"},{"key":"D","text":"units × 5100 × 5 +200 × 10 +(units - 300) × 15"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A power company charges electricity bill shown in the table below.” The correct answer is D) units × 5100 × 5 +200 × 10 +(units - 300) × 15 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) (units - 100) × 5100 × 5 +(units - 100) × 10 +(units - 200) × 15 B) (units - 100) × 5100 × 5 +200 × 10 +(units - 300) × 15 C) units × 5100 × 5 +(units - 100) × 10 +(units - 200) × 15 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":7,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In a markup language, with the purpose of displaying on a screen and printing, it is possible to directly embed not only the document content, but also the document structure and layout information, and the character font and size information. Which of the following is classified into such a markup language?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"C"},{"key":"B","text":"HTML"},{"key":"C","text":"SQL"},{"key":"D","text":"URL"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “In a markup language, with the purpose of displaying on a screen and printing, it is possible to directly embed not only the document content, but also the document structure and layout information, and the character font and size information. Which of the following is classified into such a markup language?” The correct answer is B) HTML because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) C C) SQL D) URL and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":8,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The procedure draw receives a non-negative integer number n for input. When the value of n is 6, the procedure outputs the six lines shown below. Which of the following is an appropriate combination of pieces of code to be inserted in A and B in the program?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"i ← 1i ← i + 1"},{"key":"B","text":"k ← 1k ← k + 1"},{"key":"C","text":"i ← i + 1i ← k"},{"key":"D","text":"k ← k + 1k ← i + 1"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “The procedure draw receives a non-negative integer number n for input. When the value of n is 6, the procedure outputs the six lines shown below. Which of the following is an appropriate combination of pieces of code to be inserted in A and B in the program?” The correct answer is B) k ← 1k ← k + 1 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) i ← 1i ← i + 1 C) i ← i + 1i ← k D) k ← k + 1k ← i + 1 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":9,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"On a desk that is only large enough to place four (4) files at the same time, six (6) files, A through F, are used to perform a task. When four (4) files are already placed on the desk, the least recently used file must be placed back into the drawer before the fifth file is placed on the desk. When the files are used in the sequence A, B, C, D, B, A, E, A, B, F, which of the following is the last file placed back into the drawer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"B"},{"key":"C","text":"D"},{"key":"D","text":"E"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-06.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “On a desk that is only large enough to place four (4) files at the same time, six (6) files, A through F, are used to perform a task. When four (4) files are already placed on the desk, the least recently used file must be placed back into the drawer before the fifth file is placed on the desk. When the files are used in the sequence A, B, C, D, B, A, E, A, B, F, which of the following is the last file placed back into the drawer?” The correct answer is C) D because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A B) B D) E and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":10,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When USB memory or other such external recordable media is connected to a PC, which of the following is an OS function that automatically executes programs or plays movies on the media and can also cause malware infection?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Autocorrect"},{"key":"B","text":"Autocomplete"},{"key":"C","text":"Auto filter"},{"key":"D","text":"Autorun"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-06.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When USB memory or other such external recordable media is connected to a PC, which of the following is an OS function that automatically executes programs or plays movies on the media and can also cause malware infection?” The correct answer is D) Autorun because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Autocorrect B) Autocomplete C) Auto filter and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":11,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning deep learning?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a method for studying according to proficiency level that uses textbooks published on the Internet and is not restricted by geographical location nor time."},{"key":"B","text":"A computer analyzes a large volume of data, finds patterns, and makes inferences or decisions by itself by using a neural network."},{"key":"C","text":"An appropriate response is provided based on specialist knowledge in specific fields that are systematically categorized."},{"key":"D","text":"The level of difficulty and the knowledge and skills required of each individual to solve problems are estimated according to his/her proficiency level and understanding."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning deep learning?” The correct answer is B) A computer analyzes a large volume of data, finds patterns, and makes inferences or decisions by itself by using a neural network. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) It is a method for studying according to proficiency level that uses textbooks published on the Internet and is not restricted by geographical location nor time. C) An appropriate response is provided based on specialist knowledge in specific fields that are systematically categorized. D) The level of difficulty and the knowledge and skills required of each individual to solve problems are estimated according to his/her proficiency level and understanding. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":12,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning a device driver that enables the use of peripheral devices with a PC?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"When a hard disk drive is initialized and the operating system is reinstalled, it is necessary to reinstall device drivers that were installed separately to the operating system."},{"key":"B","text":"When new application software is installed, it is necessary to reinstall all device drivers that this software uses."},{"key":"C","text":"Even if a device driver is no longer required, a user cannot delete the device driver once it is installed."},{"key":"D","text":"It is only necessary to install one (1) device driver for a printer to use all printers regardless of manufacturer or model."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning a device driver that enables the use of peripheral devices with a PC?” The correct answer is A) When a hard disk drive is initialized and the operating system is reinstalled, it is necessary to reinstall device drivers that were installed separately to the operating system. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) When new application software is installed, it is necessary to reinstall all device drivers that this software uses. C) Even if a device driver is no longer required, a user cannot delete the device driver once it is installed. D) It is only necessary to install one (1) device driver for a printer to use all printers regardless of manufacturer or model. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":13,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a description about a technology that improves the processing performance of a computer and is also called turbo boost?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is placed between the CPU and the main memory, and it remedies the slow performance of the main memory in reading and writing."},{"key":"B","text":"It increases the operation frequency of the cores when the heat that the CPU generates and the power that the CPU consumes have certain margins against their limits."},{"key":"C","text":"It provides multiple sections that serve as cores for performing calculations within the CPU, and it executes several processes simultaneously."},{"key":"D","text":"It shares the CPUs of multiple computers, and executes a large amount of processes in a distributed manner."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a description about a technology that improves the processing performance of a computer and is also called turbo boost?” The correct answer is B) It increases the operation frequency of the cores when the heat that the CPU generates and the power that the CPU consumes have certain margins against their limits. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) It is placed between the CPU and the main memory, and it remedies the slow performance of the main memory in reading and writing. C) It provides multiple sections that serve as cores for performing calculations within the CPU, and it executes several processes simultaneously. D) It shares the CPUs of multiple computers, and executes a large amount of processes in a distributed manner. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":14,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Two (2) HDDs are connected to a server for storing data. When at least one (1) of the HDDs is working, stored data needs to be available. Which of the following is an appropriate configuration that should be used for the HDDs?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Striping"},{"key":"B","text":"Data mining"},{"key":"C","text":"Tethering"},{"key":"D","text":"Mirroring"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Two (2) HDDs are connected to a server for storing data. When at least one (1) of the HDDs is working, stored data needs to be available. Which of the following is an appropriate configuration that should be used for the HDDs?” The correct answer is D) Mirroring because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Striping B) Data mining C) Tethering and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":15,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of parallel processing?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is the division of a series of processing into processing units that can be executed simultaneously, and the execution of these on multiple CPUs."},{"key":"B","text":"It is the execution of multiple related processes that are grouped together as a single process."},{"key":"C","text":"It is the performing of business logic and database processes on the server side, and the performing of user interface processes on the client side."},{"key":"D","text":"It is the division of processing time for a single CPU into short units, and the sequential allocation of these to multiple applications for execution."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of parallel processing?” The correct answer is A) It is the division of a series of processing into processing units that can be executed simultaneously, and the execution of these on multiple CPUs. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) It is the execution of multiple related processes that are grouped together as a single process. C) It is the performing of business logic and database processes on the server side, and the performing of user interface processes on the client side. D) It is the division of processing time for a single CPU into short units, and the sequential allocation of these to multiple applications for execution. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":16,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following includes all the appropriate measures to enable the execution of processing even in the event of a failure in part of a system?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(1), (3)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1), (4)"},{"key":"C","text":"(2), (3)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2), (4)"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following includes all the appropriate measures to enable the execution of processing even in the event of a failure in part of a system?” The correct answer is B) (1), (4) because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) (1), (3) C) (2), (3) D) (2), (4) and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":17,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"It is determined whether an examinee passed or failed by evaluating the score for two (2) subjects X and Y with a spreadsheet software program. The score of each subject is entered in cells A2 and B2 of the worksheet. When passing criteria (1) or (2) is met, “Pass” is displayed in cell C2, and otherwise, “Fail” is displayed. Which of the following is the expression that is entered in cell C2?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"IF(AND((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Pass', 'Fail')"},{"key":"B","text":"IF(AND((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Fail', 'Pass')"},{"key":"C","text":"IF(OR((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Pass', 'Fail')"},{"key":"D","text":"IF(OR((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Fail', 'Pass')"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “It is determined whether an examinee passed or failed by evaluating the score for two (2) subjects X and Y with a spreadsheet software program. The score of each subject is entered in cells A2 and B2 of the worksheet. When passing criteria (1) or (2) is met, “Pass” is displayed in cell C2, and otherwise, “Fail” is displayed. Which of the following is the expression that is entered in cell C2?” The correct answer is C) IF(OR((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Pass', 'Fail') because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) IF(AND((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Pass', 'Fail') B) IF(AND((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Fail', 'Pass') D) IF(OR((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Fail', 'Pass') and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":18,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through C below concerning Open Source Software (OSS), which of the following is the list that contains all and only the appropriate descriptions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"A, C"},{"key":"C","text":"B"},{"key":"D","text":"C"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among the descriptions A through C below concerning Open Source Software (OSS), which of the following is the list that contains all and only the appropriate descriptions?” The correct answer is A) A because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) A, C C) B D) C and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":19,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When directories d1 and d2 are placed on a web server as shown in the figure, which of the following descriptions specifies the reference of the web page file f2.html on directory d2 from the web page file f1.html on directory d1 (current directory)? Here, the reference method of files is as follows.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"./d2/f2.html"},{"key":"B","text":"./f2.html"},{"key":"C","text":"../d2/f2.html"},{"key":"D","text":"d2/../f2.html"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-10.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When directories d1 and d2 are placed on a web server as shown in the figure, which of the following descriptions specifies the reference of the web page file f2.html on directory d2 from the web page file f1.html on directory d1 (current directory)? Here, the reference method of files is as follows.” The correct answer is C) ../d2/f2.html because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) ./d2/f2.html B) ./f2.html D) d2/../f2.html and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":20,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The tax-inclusive prices of products A and B are calculated by using two (2) tax rates that are set in cells D2 and E2 below. The correct expression that should be entered in cell D4 is $B4*(1.0+D$2), but a wrong expression $B4*(1.0+$D$2) was entered. When the expression that was entered in cell D4 is copied to cells D5, E4, and E5, which of the following is the numeric value that is displayed in cell E5?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"525"},{"key":"B","text":"550"},{"key":"C","text":"630"},{"key":"D","text":"660"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-10.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “The tax-inclusive prices of products A and B are calculated by using two (2) tax rates that are set in cells D2 and E2 below. The correct expression that should be entered in cell D4 is $B4*(1.0+D$2), but a wrong expression $B4*(1.0+$D$2) was entered. When the expression that was entered in cell D4 is copied to cells D5, E4, and E5, which of the following is the numeric value that is displayed in cell E5?” The correct answer is C) 630 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 525 B) 550 D) 660 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":21,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a web browser that is Open Source Software (OSS)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Apache"},{"key":"B","text":"Firefox"},{"key":"C","text":"Linux"},{"key":"D","text":"Thunderbird"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-11.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a web browser that is Open Source Software (OSS)?” The correct answer is B) Firefox because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Apache C) Linux D) Thunderbird and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":22,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an OS function that executes multiple application programs concurrently on a single PC, such as when a file is downloaded from a website while data is processed with spreadsheet software?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Virtual reality"},{"key":"B","text":"Dual core"},{"key":"C","text":"Dual system"},{"key":"D","text":"Multitasking"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-11.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an OS function that executes multiple application programs concurrently on a single PC, such as when a file is downloaded from a website while data is processed with spreadsheet software?” The correct answer is D) Multitasking because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Virtual reality B) Dual core C) Dual system and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":23,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an explanation of the printing method of an inkjet printer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Printing is performed by directly spraying fine ink particles onto the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"Printing is performed by using printing pins or other such component to hit an ink ribbon against the paper."},{"key":"C","text":"Printing is performed by using the print head to heat ink that melts when it is heated."},{"key":"D","text":"Printing is performed by using laser light to make toner adhere to a photosensitive body."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an explanation of the printing method of an inkjet printer?” The correct answer is A) Printing is performed by directly spraying fine ink particles onto the paper. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Printing is performed by using printing pins or other such component to hit an ink ribbon against the paper. C) Printing is performed by using the print head to heat ink that melts when it is heated. D) Printing is performed by using laser light to make toner adhere to a photosensitive body. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":24,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the copyright protection technology that is used for a DVD-R and an SD card, and allows digital content to be duplicated to recording media only once?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AR"},{"key":"B","text":"CPRM"},{"key":"C","text":"HDMI"},{"key":"D","text":"MIDI"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the copyright protection technology that is used for a DVD-R and an SD card, and allows digital content to be duplicated to recording media only once?” The correct answer is B) CPRM because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) AR C) HDMI D) MIDI and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":25,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the unit that represents the resolution when a photograph or a picture is read by a scanner?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dpi"},{"key":"B","text":"fps"},{"key":"C","text":"pixel"},{"key":"D","text":"ppm"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the unit that represents the resolution when a photograph or a picture is read by a scanner?” The correct answer is A) dpi because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) fps C) pixel D) ppm and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":26,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"From a “Product” table and “Sales” table that are managed with a relational database, which of the following contains all and only the products where the total sales for each product in May is at least 20,000 yen?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Product A, Product B, Product C"},{"key":"B","text":"Product A, Product B, Product C, Product D"},{"key":"C","text":"Product B, Product C"},{"key":"D","text":"Product C"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “From a “Product” table and “Sales” table that are managed with a relational database, which of the following contains all and only the products where the total sales for each product in May is at least 20,000 yen?” The correct answer is C) Product B, Product C because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Product A, Product B, Product C B) Product A, Product B, Product C, Product D D) Product C and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":27,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a language used for the operation of a relational database?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"FAQ"},{"key":"B","text":"SQL"},{"key":"C","text":"SSL"},{"key":"D","text":"UML"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a language used for the operation of a relational database?” The correct answer is B) SQL because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) FAQ C) SSL D) UML and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":28,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning foreign keys in a relational database?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A property held by the foreign key is called a unique constraint."},{"key":"B","text":"Duplicate values cannot be set in the fields that are set as foreign keys."},{"key":"C","text":"Multiple foreign keys can be defined in a single table."},{"key":"D","text":"Multiple fields cannot be collectively set as a single foreign key."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning foreign keys in a relational database?” The correct answer is C) Multiple foreign keys can be defined in a single table. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A property held by the foreign key is called a unique constraint. B) Duplicate values cannot be set in the fields that are set as foreign keys. D) Multiple fields cannot be collectively set as a single foreign key. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":29,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When designing a database, which of the following is used for the purpose of organizing and representing the relation of data?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"E-R diagram"},{"key":"B","text":"Arrow diagram"},{"key":"C","text":"Gantt chart"},{"key":"D","text":"Flowchart"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When designing a database, which of the following is used for the purpose of organizing and representing the relation of data?” The correct answer is A) E-R diagram because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Arrow diagram C) Gantt chart D) Flowchart and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":30,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate combination of terms or phrases to be inserted into blanks A and B in the description below concerning NAT?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"private IP addressesa MAC address"},{"key":"B","text":"private IP addressesa global IP address"},{"key":"C","text":"host namesa MAC address"},{"key":"D","text":"host namesa global IP address"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the appropriate combination of terms or phrases to be inserted into blanks A and B in the description below concerning NAT?” The correct answer is B) private IP addressesa global IP address because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) private IP addressesa MAC address C) host namesa MAC address D) host namesa global IP address and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":31,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When another network such as the Internet is accessed from a network in an office or a household, which of the following fulfills the role of an entrance or an exit to the other network?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Splitter"},{"key":"B","text":"Default gateway"},{"key":"C","text":"Hub"},{"key":"D","text":"Repeater"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When another network such as the Internet is accessed from a network in an office or a household, which of the following fulfills the role of an entrance or an exit to the other network?” The correct answer is B) Default gateway because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Splitter C) Hub D) Repeater and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":32,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning encryption of communication when a website with the URL beginning with “https://” is browsed through a PC browser?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Only the communication from the PC to the web server is encrypted."},{"key":"B","text":"Only the communication from the web server to the PC is encrypted."},{"key":"C","text":"The bi-directional communication between the web server and PC is encrypted."},{"key":"D","text":"The direction in which communication will be encrypted depends on the settings of the web server."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning encryption of communication when a website with the URL beginning with “https://” is browsed through a PC browser?” The correct answer is C) The bi-directional communication between the web server and PC is encrypted. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Only the communication from the PC to the web server is encrypted. B) Only the communication from the web server to the PC is encrypted. D) The direction in which communication will be encrypted depends on the settings of the web server. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":33,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When transmitted over the Internet, data is divided into blocks, each of which is transmitted with a header that specifies the destination, the block number, and an error detecting code. Which of the following is the term for such blocks of data?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Domain"},{"key":"B","text":"Packet"},{"key":"C","text":"Port"},{"key":"D","text":"Router"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When transmitted over the Internet, data is divided into blocks, each of which is transmitted with a header that specifies the destination, the block number, and an error detecting code. Which of the following is the term for such blocks of data?” The correct answer is B) Packet because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Domain C) Port D) Router and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":34,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A DHCP server has been installed in a LAN. When a PC that automatically acquires information from the DHCP server is to be connected to the LAN, which of the following will be set in the PC?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"IP address"},{"key":"B","text":"Latest virus definition file"},{"key":"C","text":"Address list of spam mail"},{"key":"D","text":"Mail addresses assigned by the Internet service provider"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A DHCP server has been installed in a LAN. When a PC that automatically acquires information from the DHCP server is to be connected to the LAN, which of the following will be set in the PC?” The correct answer is A) IP address because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Latest virus definition file C) Address list of spam mail D) Mail addresses assigned by the Internet service provider and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":35,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate example of biometric authentication?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Displaying an image of characters that are difficult for a machine to read on a monitor, and having a person read the characters and enter them"},{"key":"B","text":"Having a person enter a password via a software keyboard that is displayed on a touch panel"},{"key":"C","text":"Reading the trail, pressure, and other characteristics of the action when a touch pen is used for a signature"},{"key":"D","text":"Having a person answer a question that only the person knows the answer to"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the appropriate example of biometric authentication?” The correct answer is C) Reading the trail, pressure, and other characteristics of the action when a touch pen is used for a signature because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Displaying an image of characters that are difficult for a machine to read on a monitor, and having a person read the characters and enter them B) Having a person enter a password via a software keyboard that is displayed on a touch panel D) Having a person answer a question that only the person knows the answer to and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":36,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When a document file attached to a received e-mail is opened on a PC, the PC begins to behave abnormally. Which of the following is an appropriate suspected attack?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"SQL injection"},{"key":"B","text":"Cross-site scripting"},{"key":"C","text":"Shoulder hacking"},{"key":"D","text":"Macro virus"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When a document file attached to a received e-mail is opened on a PC, the PC begins to behave abnormally. Which of the following is an appropriate suspected attack?” The correct answer is D) Macro virus because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) SQL injection B) Cross-site scripting C) Shoulder hacking and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":37,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the activity in A (Act) phase in the PDCA model adopted in an organization that operates an ISMS?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Deciding to make improvements concerning matters such as flaws that are revealed through the monitoring of operational status and the measurement and evaluation of operational results"},{"key":"B","text":"Monitoring operational status, and measuring and evaluating operational results"},{"key":"C","text":"Creating a security policy, establishing an organizational structure, and creating a procedure for achieving the targets that are defined in the security policy"},{"key":"D","text":"Communicating the security policy to employees, installing security equipment and other security measures, and operating them"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the activity in A (Act) phase in the PDCA model adopted in an organization that operates an ISMS?” The correct answer is A) Deciding to make improvements concerning matters such as flaws that are revealed through the monitoring of operational status and the measurement and evaluation of operational results because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Monitoring operational status, and measuring and evaluating operational results C) Creating a security policy, establishing an organizational structure, and creating a procedure for achieving the targets that are defined in the security policy D) Communicating the security policy to employees, installing security equipment and other security measures, and operating them and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":38,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an example of an aim of an attacker who infects someone else’s PC with ransomware?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To obtain personal information on the PC via a network"},{"key":"B","text":"To make files on the PC unusable, and to obtain money in exchange from unlocking them"},{"key":"C","text":"To obtain characters typed with the PC keyboard via a network"},{"key":"D","text":"To operate the PC without the user’s permission by sending instructions for operations via a network"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an example of an aim of an attacker who infects someone else’s PC with ransomware?” The correct answer is B) To make files on the PC unusable, and to obtain money in exchange from unlocking them because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) To obtain personal information on the PC via a network C) To obtain characters typed with the PC keyboard via a network D) To operate the PC without the user’s permission by sending instructions for operations via a network and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":39,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A private key and a public key were generated as a key pair and a digital certificate for the public key was issued. Which of the following is an appropriate action that should be taken when the private key is leaked?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Reissuing the digital certificate with the same key pair"},{"key":"B","text":"Requesting to the certification authority for revocation of the digital certificate"},{"key":"C","text":"Creating a new key pair for reissuing a certificate due to the expiration of the validity period"},{"key":"D","text":"Continuing using the same digital certificate, because only the private key was leaked"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A private key and a public key were generated as a key pair and a digital certificate for the public key was issued. Which of the following is an appropriate action that should be taken when the private key is leaked?” The correct answer is B) Requesting to the certification authority for revocation of the digital certificate because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Reissuing the digital certificate with the same key pair C) Creating a new key pair for reissuing a certificate due to the expiration of the validity period D) Continuing using the same digital certificate, because only the private key was leaked and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":40,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following sets conditions for character type, length, etc. used for passwords that are set for accounts on a computer, etc.?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Single sign-on"},{"key":"B","text":"Password crack"},{"key":"C","text":"Password policy"},{"key":"D","text":"One-time password"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following sets conditions for character type, length, etc. used for passwords that are set for accounts on a computer, etc.?” The correct answer is C) Password policy because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Single sign-on B) Password crack D) One-time password and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":41,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among confidentiality, integrity, and availability, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the properties that are lost in the information security incident below?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Confidentiality"},{"key":"B","text":"Confidentiality, integrity"},{"key":"C","text":"Integrity, availability"},{"key":"D","text":"Availability"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among confidentiality, integrity, and availability, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the properties that are lost in the information security incident below?” The correct answer is C) Integrity, availability because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Confidentiality B) Confidentiality, integrity D) Availability and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":42,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A problem has been pointed out that the WEP encryption for wireless LANs can be broken easily. Which of the following is an encryption method that does not have the same weakness and is cryptographically stronger?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ESSID"},{"key":"B","text":"S/MIME"},{"key":"C","text":"SSL"},{"key":"D","text":"WPA2"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A problem has been pointed out that the WEP encryption for wireless LANs can be broken easily. Which of the following is an encryption method that does not have the same weakness and is cryptographically stronger?” The correct answer is D) WPA2 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) ESSID B) S/MIME C) SSL and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":43,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Company A implements risk analysis for its own information assets. The results show that if a nearby river overflows, the server room on the first floor of the company might be flooded. The company considers the possibility of moving the server room, but decides there is almost no risk of a flood because the last time the river overflowed was 100 years ago, and the management decides that no particular countermeasures are taken. Which of the following is the risk treatment for information security that Company A selects?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Risk transfer"},{"key":"B","text":"Risk avoidance"},{"key":"C","text":"Risk acceptance"},{"key":"D","text":"Risk mitigation"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Company A implements risk analysis for its own information assets. The results show that if a nearby river overflows, the server room on the first floor of the company might be flooded. The company considers the possibility of moving the server room, but decides there is almost no risk of a flood because the last time the river overflowed was 100 years ago, and the management decides that no particular countermeasures are taken. Which of the following is the risk treatment for information security that Company A selects?” The correct answer is C) Risk acceptance because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Risk transfer B) Risk avoidance D) Risk mitigation and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":44,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The decision is made to digitize a paper-based contact list that only some people are permitted to view, and to manage it as a contact file. Among the measures A through D below, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the appropriate measures against personal information leakage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “The decision is made to digitize a paper-based contact list that only some people are permitted to view, and to manage it as a contact file. Among the measures A through D below, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the appropriate measures against personal information leakage?” The correct answer is C) A, B, D because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A, B B) A, B, C D) C, D and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":45,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the Web browsing practices (1) through (3) below, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the practices that reduce security risks?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(1), (2)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1), (3)"},{"key":"C","text":"(2)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2), (3)"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among the Web browsing practices (1) through (3) below, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the practices that reduce security risks?” The correct answer is C) (2) because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) (1), (2) B) (1), (3) D) (2), (3) and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":46,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In software development, which of the following is the appropriate combination of the descriptions A through C concerning testing and testing processes?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ABC"},{"key":"B","text":"ACB"},{"key":"C","text":"BAC"},{"key":"D","text":"CBA"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “In software development, which of the following is the appropriate combination of the descriptions A through C concerning testing and testing processes?” The correct answer is D) CBA because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) ABC B) ACB C) BAC and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":47,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following corresponds to software maintenance?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A response time that was measured in a system test did not satisfy the requirement, so tuning was performed on the software."},{"key":"B","text":"As a result of a software acceptance test, a defect was found, so the orderer requested the developer to fix the software."},{"key":"C","text":"A function was found missing in a unit test of a program, so the function was added to the program."},{"key":"D","text":"A defect was reported on software that is running on a production system, so the software was modified."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following corresponds to software maintenance?” The correct answer is D) A defect was reported on software that is running on a production system, so the software was modified. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A response time that was measured in a system test did not satisfy the requirement, so tuning was performed on the software. B) As a result of a software acceptance test, a defect was found, so the orderer requested the developer to fix the software. C) A function was found missing in a unit test of a program, so the function was added to the program. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":48,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate test for a user to confirm by himself/herself whether the delivered software satisfies the requirements?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Acceptance test"},{"key":"B","text":"Integration test"},{"key":"C","text":"System test"},{"key":"D","text":"Unit test"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate test for a user to confirm by himself/herself whether the delivered software satisfies the requirements?” The correct answer is A) Acceptance test because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Integration test C) System test D) Unit test and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":49,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A system migration plan was created for the migration from an existing system to a new system. Which of the following is an appropriate item to be described in the system migration plan?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"System selection policy"},{"key":"B","text":"Schedule for parallel operation of the existing and new systems"},{"key":"C","text":"Evaluation criteria for the quality of the deliverables"},{"key":"D","text":"The work history of project members"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A system migration plan was created for the migration from an existing system to a new system. Which of the following is an appropriate item to be described in the system migration plan?” The correct answer is B) Schedule for parallel operation of the existing and new systems because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) System selection policy C) Evaluation criteria for the quality of the deliverables D) The work history of project members and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":50,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of refactoring?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Improving internal architecture without changing the functions that software provides"},{"key":"B","text":"Discovering the specifications of software by analysis of its operations, etc."},{"key":"C","text":"Correcting a defect in software so that it performs according to the specifications"},{"key":"D","text":"Modifying software to add a new function on the basis of user requests, etc."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of refactoring?” The correct answer is A) Improving internal architecture without changing the functions that software provides because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Discovering the specifications of software by analysis of its operations, etc. C) Correcting a defect in software so that it performs according to the specifications D) Modifying software to add a new function on the basis of user requests, etc. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":51,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through D below concerning project management in system development, which of the following lists all and only the failures in scope management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among the descriptions A through D below concerning project management in system development, which of the following lists all and only the failures in scope management?” The correct answer is D) C, D because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A, B B) B, C C) B, D and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":52,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"For software development work, a plan is created to complete it with 10 people in a period of 15 days. However, it became known that only eight (8) members of staff could be obtained for the first five (5) days. In order to complete the work in 15 days as planned, how many staff members are required from the 6-th day? Here, the productivity of each member of staff is the same.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"11"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"14"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “For software development work, a plan is created to complete it with 10 people in a period of 15 days. However, it became known that only eight (8) members of staff could be obtained for the first five (5) days. In order to complete the work in 15 days as planned, how many staff members are required from the 6-th day? Here, the productivity of each member of staff is the same.” The correct answer is B) 11 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 10 C) 12 D) 14 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":53,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning risk management in a project?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Since a project has a predetermined deadline, all risks must be identified at the start of the project."},{"key":"B","text":"Since the realization of a risk has a negative impact to a project, risk measures are planned to avoid all risks."},{"key":"C","text":"In order to plan risk measures, risks are prioritized on the basis of the likelihood of occurrence of an event and its consequences."},{"key":"D","text":"In order to cut down the cost involved in taking action against a risk, risk measures are planned whenever a risk is realized."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning risk management in a project?” The correct answer is C) In order to plan risk measures, risks are prioritized on the basis of the likelihood of occurrence of an event and its consequences. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Since a project has a predetermined deadline, all risks must be identified at the start of the project. B) Since the realization of a risk has a negative impact to a project, risk measures are planned to avoid all risks. D) In order to cut down the cost involved in taking action against a risk, risk measures are planned whenever a risk is realized. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":54,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A company orders information system development to an overseas software developer under a contract for software development. Which of the following is an appropriate activity to be performed by the company in project procurement management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"When a defect is found after the acceptance of delivery, even if not indicated in the contract, the company asks the developer to examine not only the defect but similar defects and fix them."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to make good use of the capabilities of the developer, the company does not include the provisions of intellectual property rights in the contract."},{"key":"C","text":"After the start of development, the company has the procurement detail such as the development scope, specifications, and work contents, etc. agreed upon by the developer in writing."},{"key":"D","text":"At the time of signing the contract, the company agrees upon in writing with the developer the documents to be delivered and the rules for changing specifications during development."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A company orders information system development to an overseas software developer under a contract for software development. Which of the following is an appropriate activity to be performed by the company in project procurement management?” The correct answer is D) At the time of signing the contract, the company agrees upon in writing with the developer the documents to be delivered and the rules for changing specifications during development. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) When a defect is found after the acceptance of delivery, even if not indicated in the contract, the company asks the developer to examine not only the defect but similar defects and fix them. B) In order to make good use of the capabilities of the developer, the company does not include the provisions of intellectual property rights in the contract. C) After the start of development, the company has the procurement detail such as the development scope, specifications, and work contents, etc. agreed upon by the developer in writing. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":55,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a method to break down the required activities into a hierarchical structure in software development?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"CMM"},{"key":"B","text":"ITIL"},{"key":"C","text":"PERT"},{"key":"D","text":"WBS"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a method to break down the required activities into a hierarchical structure in software development?” The correct answer is D) WBS because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) CMM B) ITIL C) PERT and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":56,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Quality management in system development projects has a quality planning process to define quality requirements and quality standards for deliverables and to specify the methods for achieving them. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the quality planning process?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"If deliverables are not exactly the same as those of past system development projects, past quality standards cannot be used as reference."},{"key":"B","text":"Since schedules have the highest priority in all projects, it is acceptable to shorten the period for reviewing and testing for achieving target quality."},{"key":"C","text":"Quality should have the highest priory in all projects, and, to enhance the quality of deliverables, constraints should not be placed on the budget."},{"key":"D","text":"The effects such as reductions in reworking, improvement in productivity, improvement of stakeholder satisfaction brought about by achieving targeted quality, and the required costs are to be compared."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Quality management in system development projects has a quality planning process to define quality requirements and quality standards for deliverables and to specify the methods for achieving them. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the quality planning process?” The correct answer is D) The effects such as reductions in reworking, improvement in productivity, improvement of stakeholder satisfaction brought about by achieving targeted quality, and the required costs are to be compared. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) If deliverables are not exactly the same as those of past system development projects, past quality standards cannot be used as reference. B) Since schedules have the highest priority in all projects, it is acceptable to shorten the period for reviewing and testing for achieving target quality. C) Quality should have the highest priory in all projects, and, to enhance the quality of deliverables, constraints should not be placed on the budget. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":57,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In a project, a contingency reserve is the cost that is included in the initial project scope and is prepared for events that are predictable but uncertain. Among the costs that are allocated by the project manager of a company that receives an order for a system development, which of the following is an appropriate cost that can be classified as a contingency reserve?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The cost that is necessary for the replacement of a device when the device happens to fail under the development environment"},{"key":"B","text":"The cost that is necessary for the activities of the project leader who manages the development progress"},{"key":"C","text":"The cost that is necessary for fulfilling the new requirements of users that are outside the scope of the project"},{"key":"D","text":"The cost that is necessary for purchasing the quality management tools of a system that are planned to be adopted in the project"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “In a project, a contingency reserve is the cost that is included in the initial project scope and is prepared for events that are predictable but uncertain. Among the costs that are allocated by the project manager of a company that receives an order for a system development, which of the following is an appropriate cost that can be classified as a contingency reserve?” The correct answer is A) The cost that is necessary for the replacement of a device when the device happens to fail under the development environment because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) The cost that is necessary for the activities of the project leader who manages the development progress C) The cost that is necessary for fulfilling the new requirements of users that are outside the scope of the project D) The cost that is necessary for purchasing the quality management tools of a system that are planned to be adopted in the project and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":58,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In a service desk that acts as the point of contact for users, a tool that uses automated response technology is used in addition to telephone and e-mail. Which of the following is the most appropriate example of such a tool?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"FAQ"},{"key":"B","text":"RPA"},{"key":"C","text":"Escalation"},{"key":"D","text":"Chatbot"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “In a service desk that acts as the point of contact for users, a tool that uses automated response technology is used in addition to telephone and e-mail. Which of the following is the most appropriate example of such a tool?” The correct answer is D) Chatbot because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) FAQ B) RPA C) Escalation and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":59,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate requirement for the availability of an e-mail service in IT service management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Allowing the e-mail service to be used with only a web browser"},{"key":"B","text":"Allowing the e-mail service to be used anytime except for defined maintenance hours"},{"key":"C","text":"Preventing e-mails addressed to a user from being read by another user without permission"},{"key":"D","text":"Preventing sent e-mails from being falsified"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate requirement for the availability of an e-mail service in IT service management?” The correct answer is B) Allowing the e-mail service to be used anytime except for defined maintenance hours because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Allowing the e-mail service to be used with only a web browser C) Preventing e-mails addressed to a user from being read by another user without permission D) Preventing sent e-mails from being falsified and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":60,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate purpose of providing FAQ to users in IT service management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Providing a framework of IT service management"},{"key":"B","text":"Defining a target value for the service level on the sides of both service provider and users"},{"key":"C","text":"Establishing a single point of contact for users to make all kinds of queries concerning the service"},{"key":"D","text":"Supporting users so that they can solve problems by themselves"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-27.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate purpose of providing FAQ to users in IT service management?” The correct answer is D) Supporting users so that they can solve problems by themselves because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Providing a framework of IT service management B) Defining a target value for the service level on the sides of both service provider and users C) Establishing a single point of contact for users to make all kinds of queries concerning the service and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":61,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through D below, which of the following lists all and only the activities of facility management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, C"},{"key":"B","text":"A, D"},{"key":"C","text":"B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-27.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among the descriptions A through D below, which of the following lists all and only the activities of facility management?” The correct answer is B) A, D because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A, C C) B, D D) C, D and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":62,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate example of criteria for evaluating the service level of a service desk that receives queries from system users over the telephone?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Cost of the service"},{"key":"B","text":"Number of system failures"},{"key":"C","text":"Availability of the system"},{"key":"D","text":"Response time for queries"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate example of criteria for evaluating the service level of a service desk that receives queries from system users over the telephone?” The correct answer is D) Response time for queries because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Cost of the service B) Number of system failures C) Availability of the system and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":63,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of monitoring in internal control?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a process of continuously evaluating if internal control is working effectively."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a process of promoting compliance to the laws and other regulations concerning internal control."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a process of establishing an organization for internal control."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a process of analyzing the risks that hinder internal control."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of monitoring in internal control?” The correct answer is A) It is a process of continuously evaluating if internal control is working effectively. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) It is a process of promoting compliance to the laws and other regulations concerning internal control. C) It is a process of establishing an organization for internal control. D) It is a process of analyzing the risks that hinder internal control. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":64,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate measure to enable internal controls?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Preventing creation of a job description indicating the scope of work and roles"},{"key":"B","text":"Preventing creation of a work handover document for a successor"},{"key":"C","text":"Preventing processing of purchasing and payment by the same person"},{"key":"D","text":"Preventing separation of team members for system development and system operation"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate measure to enable internal controls?” The correct answer is C) Preventing processing of purchasing and payment by the same person because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Preventing creation of a job description indicating the scope of work and roles B) Preventing creation of a work handover document for a successor D) Preventing separation of team members for system development and system operation and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":65,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description of the roles of a system auditor?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Preparing a workflow, work description, and risk control matrix that reflect the flow and business operations, evaluating the risks, and installing an appropriate system"},{"key":"B","text":"Installing a mechanism for appropriate monitoring and self-inspection in each process of planning, development, operation, and maintenance of the information system, and taking actions to operate the information system smoothly"},{"key":"C","text":"Verifying whether or not the risks of the information system are controlled appropriately and effectively from a standpoint that is independent of the department being audited, and reporting the result to the client"},{"key":"D","text":"Specifying the policies and objectives, and establishing a management system so that the risks of the information system are controlled appropriately"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate description of the roles of a system auditor?” The correct answer is C) Verifying whether or not the risks of the information system are controlled appropriately and effectively from a standpoint that is independent of the department being audited, and reporting the result to the client because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Preparing a workflow, work description, and risk control matrix that reflect the flow and business operations, evaluating the risks, and installing an appropriate system B) Installing a mechanism for appropriate monitoring and self-inspection in each process of planning, development, operation, and maintenance of the information system, and taking actions to operate the information system smoothly D) Specifying the policies and objectives, and establishing a management system so that the risks of the information system are controlled appropriately and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":66,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Company A is a large company with multiple offices nationwide, and it created BCP that envisaged the total destruction of the head office building in a large natural disaster. In consideration of the purpose of the BCP, which of the following is Company A’s most appropriate BCP?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In order to prevent damage by a fire that occurs after a disaster, replacing curtains and other such things with flame-resistant products and planning regular checks of fire prevention equipment"},{"key":"B","text":"In order to swiftly respond to instructions from the head office when a disaster occurs, establishing a procedure to completely halting work at all offices and have all employees standby until an instruction is received from the head office"},{"key":"C","text":"In order to continue business after a natural disaster, specifying an office to take over the functions of the head office, narrowing down the important work that needs to be dealt with, and establishing an implementation procedure for this work"},{"key":"D","text":"Incorporating insurance premiums for the head office building into the annual budget, and preparing for a relocation to a building with the same scale as the current head office"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Company A is a large company with multiple offices nationwide, and it created BCP that envisaged the total destruction of the head office building in a large natural disaster. In consideration of the purpose of the BCP, which of the following is Company A’s most appropriate BCP?” The correct answer is C) In order to continue business after a natural disaster, specifying an office to take over the functions of the head office, narrowing down the important work that needs to be dealt with, and establishing an implementation procedure for this work because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) In order to prevent damage by a fire that occurs after a disaster, replacing curtains and other such things with flame-resistant products and planning regular checks of fire prevention equipment B) In order to swiftly respond to instructions from the head office when a disaster occurs, establishing a procedure to completely halting work at all offices and have all employees standby until an instruction is received from the head office D) Incorporating insurance premiums for the head office building into the annual budget, and preparing for a relocation to a building with the same scale as the current head office and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":67,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an explanation of a balance sheet?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It displays the status of cash flow in a fixed period of time by activity category."},{"key":"B","text":"It displays the management performance of a company by the income and cost generated in a fixed period of time."},{"key":"C","text":"It displays the previous term-end balance, changes during the year, and the current term-end balance for each item of net assets of a company."},{"key":"D","text":"It displays the financial condition of a company on the date of settlement on the basis of the categories of assets, liabilities, and net assets."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an explanation of a balance sheet?” The correct answer is D) It displays the financial condition of a company on the date of settlement on the basis of the categories of assets, liabilities, and net assets. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) It displays the status of cash flow in a fixed period of time by activity category. B) It displays the management performance of a company by the income and cost generated in a fixed period of time. C) It displays the previous term-end balance, changes during the year, and the current term-end balance for each item of net assets of a company. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":68,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The operating profit when the sales quantity of a product is 700 units is as shown in the table below. When the unit sales price is reduced by 20% to expand sales, the sales quantity increases by 20%. How much, in yen, is the operating profit at this time? Here, the variable cost per one (1) unit of the product does not change.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"200,000"},{"key":"B","text":"204,000"},{"key":"C","text":"260,000"},{"key":"D","text":"320,000"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “The operating profit when the sales quantity of a product is 700 units is as shown in the table below. When the unit sales price is reduced by 20% to expand sales, the sales quantity increases by 20%. How much, in yen, is the operating profit at this time? Here, the variable cost per one (1) unit of the product does not change.” The correct answer is B) 204,000 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 200,000 C) 260,000 D) 320,000 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":69,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the phases of the PDCA cycle in corporate business operations, which of the following measures and evaluates the status of operations on the basis of KPI?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"P"},{"key":"B","text":"D"},{"key":"C","text":"C"},{"key":"D","text":"A"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among the phases of the PDCA cycle in corporate business operations, which of the following measures and evaluates the status of operations on the basis of KPI?” The correct answer is C) C because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) P B) D D) A and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":70,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Data of the defects and faults of products, complaints from customers, etc. are categorized according to their cause and situation. Which of the following represents the number of data in each category in descending order on a bar graph and the cumulative total on a line graph?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Control chart"},{"key":"B","text":"Tree diagram"},{"key":"C","text":"Pareto chart"},{"key":"D","text":"Matrix chart"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Data of the defects and faults of products, complaints from customers, etc. are categorized according to their cause and situation. Which of the following represents the number of data in each category in descending order on a bar graph and the cumulative total on a line graph?” The correct answer is C) Pareto chart because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Control chart B) Tree diagram D) Matrix chart and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":71,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When the purchase and sales of a product in April are as in the table below, what is the inventory value in yen for the product at the end of April according to the moving average method? The moving average method calculates the average unit price of products in the inventory each time a purchase is made, and uses the average unit price for products in the inventory immediately beforehand for the calculation of the inventory value.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"1,280"},{"key":"B","text":"1,300"},{"key":"C","text":"1,400"},{"key":"D","text":"1,500"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When the purchase and sales of a product in April are as in the table below, what is the inventory value in yen for the product at the end of April according to the moving average method? The moving average method calculates the average unit price of products in the inventory each time a purchase is made, and uses the average unit price for products in the inventory immediately beforehand for the calculation of the inventory value.” The correct answer is C) 1,400 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 1,280 B) 1,300 D) 1,500 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":72,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A person wishes to start at point X, pass through all of points A, B, and C, and arrive at point Y. When the routes and the required times between points are as shown in the figure and the table, what is the shortest time in minutes from point X to point Y? Here, the points A, B, and C may be passed through in any order.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"110"},{"key":"B","text":"130"},{"key":"C","text":"140"},{"key":"D","text":"150"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A person wishes to start at point X, pass through all of points A, B, and C, and arrive at point Y. When the routes and the required times between points are as shown in the figure and the table, what is the shortest time in minutes from point X to point Y? Here, the points A, B, and C may be passed through in any order.” The correct answer is B) 130 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 110 C) 140 D) 150 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":73,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description of NDA?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a specialized organization that monitors and analyzes threats to the information systems in a company, etc."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a contract that makes the contracting parties agree to hold and maintain in confidence the confidential information of the other party."},{"key":"C","text":"It is an agreement of an objective quality standard that is concluded between a service provider and the user concerning the service provided."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a hierarchical decomposition of the tasks to be implemented in a project."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate description of NDA?” The correct answer is B) It is a contract that makes the contracting parties agree to hold and maintain in confidence the confidential information of the other party. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) It is a specialized organization that monitors and analyzes threats to the information systems in a company, etc. C) It is an agreement of an objective quality standard that is concluded between a service provider and the user concerning the service provided. D) It is a hierarchical decomposition of the tasks to be implemented in a project. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":74,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a code that stores information in a vertical and horizontal two-dimensional pattern?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ASCII code"},{"key":"B","text":"G-code"},{"key":"C","text":"EAN code"},{"key":"D","text":"QR code"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a code that stores information in a vertical and horizontal two-dimensional pattern?” The correct answer is D) QR code because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) ASCII code B) G-code C) EAN code and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":75,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Concerning the EU’s General Data Protection Rules (GDPR), which of the following lists all and only the appropriate descriptions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, C"},{"key":"D","text":"A, C, D"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Concerning the EU’s General Data Protection Rules (GDPR), which of the following lists all and only the appropriate descriptions?” The correct answer is C) A, C because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A B) A, B, C D) A, C, D and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":76,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among company’s actions A through C below, which of the following lists all and only the acts that may be problematic in terms of compliance?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, C"},{"key":"D","text":"B, C"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Among company’s actions A through C below, which of the following lists all and only the acts that may be problematic in terms of compliance?” The correct answer is D) B, C because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) A, B B) A, B, C C) A, C and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":77,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is appropriate as an expected advantage of the adoption of ISO 9001 by companies?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The companies’ trade procedures will be standardized, leading to increased efficiency and the avoidance of non-tariff barriers."},{"key":"B","text":"Technical specifications will be standardized in the industry, and increase in product quality and expansion of markets will move forward."},{"key":"C","text":"Methods for handling information assets will be standardized and the quality of information security will increase."},{"key":"D","text":"Business operations concerning quality management will be standardized, and the quality and efficiency of management will increase."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is appropriate as an expected advantage of the adoption of ISO 9001 by companies?” The correct answer is D) Business operations concerning quality management will be standardized, and the quality and efficiency of management will increase. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) The companies’ trade procedures will be standardized, leading to increased efficiency and the avoidance of non-tariff barriers. B) Technical specifications will be standardized in the industry, and increase in product quality and expansion of markets will move forward. C) Methods for handling information assets will be standardized and the quality of information security will increase. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":78,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an organization in the USA that promotes standardization activities concerning Ethernet LAN and wireless LAN, etc.?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ICANN"},{"key":"B","text":"IEEE"},{"key":"C","text":"ISO"},{"key":"D","text":"W3C"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an organization in the USA that promotes standardization activities concerning Ethernet LAN and wireless LAN, etc.?” The correct answer is B) IEEE because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) ICANN C) ISO D) W3C and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":79,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate marketing strategy for narrowing down the customer base to focus on by classifying customers on the basis of age, gender, family structure, and the like, and analyzing the purchasing behaviors of each group?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Service marketing"},{"key":"B","text":"Segment marketing"},{"key":"C","text":"Social marketing"},{"key":"D","text":"Mass marketing"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate marketing strategy for narrowing down the customer base to focus on by classifying customers on the basis of age, gender, family structure, and the like, and analyzing the purchasing behaviors of each group?” The correct answer is B) Segment marketing because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Service marketing C) Social marketing D) Mass marketing and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":80,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"There are two (2) indicators for evaluating the achievement of strategic goals. These are leading indicators that evaluate the means for achieving the goals, and result indicators that evaluate the degree of goal achievement. If a strategic goal is “acquire new customers,” which of the following is an appropriate leading indicator?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sales increase amount"},{"key":"B","text":"New contract acquisition ratio"},{"key":"C","text":"Total customer increase ratio"},{"key":"D","text":"Number of visits to prospective customers"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “There are two (2) indicators for evaluating the achievement of strategic goals. These are leading indicators that evaluate the means for achieving the goals, and result indicators that evaluate the degree of goal achievement. If a strategic goal is “acquire new customers,” which of the following is an appropriate leading indicator?” The correct answer is D) Number of visits to prospective customers because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Sales increase amount B) New contract acquisition ratio C) Total customer increase ratio and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":81,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of user experience (UX)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The design of a software product with consideration that it is easy to use for as many people as possible, including mainly elderly people and disabled people"},{"key":"B","text":"A method of identifying customers on the basis of analysis of customer data, and deepening relationships with customers by using channels such as call centers and the Internet"},{"key":"C","text":"A software product’s capability that enables efficient use by a user under specified conditions"},{"key":"D","text":"People’s feelings and responses that are gained through the use of a product, system, or service"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of user experience (UX)?” The correct answer is D) People’s feelings and responses that are gained through the use of a product, system, or service because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) The design of a software product with consideration that it is easy to use for as many people as possible, including mainly elderly people and disabled people B) A method of identifying customers on the basis of analysis of customer data, and deepening relationships with customers by using channels such as call centers and the Internet C) A software product’s capability that enables efficient use by a user under specified conditions and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":82,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a system that centrally manages the process from materials procurement to product sales, and aims for the optimization of supply?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ASP"},{"key":"B","text":"CRM"},{"key":"C","text":"ERP"},{"key":"D","text":"SCM"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a system that centrally manages the process from materials procurement to product sales, and aims for the optimization of supply?” The correct answer is D) SCM because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) ASP B) CRM C) ERP and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":83,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Company A performs analysis of its positioning with competitors. In order for Company A to obtain the best evaluation of all three (3) companies, what is the minimum number of points required in the brand evaluation item?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"9"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Company A performs analysis of its positioning with competitors. In order for Company A to obtain the best evaluation of all three (3) companies, what is the minimum number of points required in the brand evaluation item?” The correct answer is C) 8 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 6 B) 7 D) 9 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":84,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate as the underlying concept of CRM?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The source of profit is an early entry into a market with little competition."},{"key":"B","text":"The source of profit is a good relationship with the customer."},{"key":"C","text":"The source of profit is a shorter product life cycle."},{"key":"D","text":"The source of profit is a large share in a specific market."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate as the underlying concept of CRM?” The correct answer is B) The source of profit is a good relationship with the customer. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) The source of profit is an early entry into a market with little competition. C) The source of profit is a shorter product life cycle. D) The source of profit is a large share in a specific market. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":85,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a technique that increases the potential for success in the development of a new business model or product, by creating the minimum service or product on the basis of a hypothesis, and performing repeated verification of customer value in a short interval of times?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Cannibalization"},{"key":"B","text":"Business operations modeling"},{"key":"C","text":"Digital transformation"},{"key":"D","text":"Lean startup"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a technique that increases the potential for success in the development of a new business model or product, by creating the minimum service or product on the basis of a hypothesis, and performing repeated verification of customer value in a short interval of times?” The correct answer is D) Lean startup because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Cannibalization B) Business operations modeling C) Digital transformation and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":86,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In call handling at a call center, which of the following is the most appropriate example of the use of AI to implement a more effective FAQ system?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As part of the training for operators, examples of questions and answers that use the existing FAQ are taught on a web screen."},{"key":"B","text":"According to the numbers that are entered according to the guidance, a call is assigned to an operator with responsibility for the relevant FAQ item."},{"key":"C","text":"From the caller’s telephone number of a received call, customer information and a record of the content and response of past inquiries are retrieved from a customer information database and displayed on the operator’s screen."},{"key":"D","text":"In call handling, emotion and intent are determined from the audio of a question in order to increase the certainty of selection of the optimum candidate response from the FAQ."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “In call handling at a call center, which of the following is the most appropriate example of the use of AI to implement a more effective FAQ system?” The correct answer is D) In call handling, emotion and intent are determined from the audio of a question in order to increase the certainty of selection of the optimum candidate response from the FAQ. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) As part of the training for operators, examples of questions and answers that use the existing FAQ are taught on a web screen. B) According to the numbers that are entered according to the guidance, a call is assigned to an operator with responsibility for the relevant FAQ item. C) From the caller’s telephone number of a received call, customer information and a record of the content and response of past inquiries are retrieved from a customer information database and displayed on the operator’s screen. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":87,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a business objective that becomes possible to achieve with “the introduction of a POS system”?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Improvement in the work productivity of salespersons and organizational strength of the sales department"},{"key":"B","text":"Reduction in inventory volume of component parts and partly finished goods"},{"key":"C","text":"Optimization of the series of processes from procurement to manufacturing, shipment, and sales"},{"key":"D","text":"Improvement in the selection of goods at each store and streamlining of ordering and inventory control"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-38.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is a business objective that becomes possible to achieve with “the introduction of a POS system”?” The correct answer is D) Improvement in the selection of goods at each store and streamlining of ordering and inventory control because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Improvement in the work productivity of salespersons and organizational strength of the sales department B) Reduction in inventory volume of component parts and partly finished goods C) Optimization of the series of processes from procurement to manufacturing, shipment, and sales and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":88,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of CAD, as used in the manufacturing industry?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It calculates the required quantity of materials for a product manufacturing plan and orders materials."},{"key":"B","text":"It manages information about the components, semi-finished products, quantities, etc. required for the manufacture of products."},{"key":"C","text":"It performs unified management of information such as product blueprints and component tables, from design to manufacturing."},{"key":"D","text":"It uses computers in product design to improve the productivity and reliability of design specifications."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-38.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of CAD, as used in the manufacturing industry?” The correct answer is D) It uses computers in product design to improve the productivity and reliability of design specifications. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) It calculates the required quantity of materials for a product manufacturing plan and orders materials. B) It manages information about the components, semi-finished products, quantities, etc. required for the manufacture of products. C) It performs unified management of information such as product blueprints and component tables, from design to manufacturing. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":89,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate case example that corresponds to traceability?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Taking advantage of the Internet and web technology for the use of computers in education"},{"key":"B","text":"Outsourcing all software development to an external specialized company without placing any development department within one’s own company"},{"key":"C","text":"Sharing knowledge and information among employees across the entire organization, and utilizing it effectively to improve business performance"},{"key":"D","text":"Being able to check the history from production up to sales on the basis of the labels pasted on meat and fish products"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-39.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is an appropriate case example that corresponds to traceability?” The correct answer is D) Being able to check the history from production up to sales on the basis of the labels pasted on meat and fish products because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) Taking advantage of the Internet and web technology for the use of computers in education B) Outsourcing all software development to an external specialized company without placing any development department within one’s own company C) Sharing knowledge and information among employees across the entire organization, and utilizing it effectively to improve business performance and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":90,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is classified as a “B to E” transaction?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A company provides services, such as welfare and education for the company’s own employees, through the Internet."},{"key":"B","text":"A travel company uses the Internet to give campaign information and sell tickets to consumers in advance."},{"key":"C","text":"An automobile manufacturer uses the Internet to procure components and materials from vendors across the world."},{"key":"D","text":"In an auction held on the Internet, a participant buys a product from another participant."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-39.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is classified as a “B to E” transaction?” The correct answer is A) A company provides services, such as welfare and education for the company’s own employees, through the Internet. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) A travel company uses the Internet to give campaign information and sell tickets to consumers in advance. C) An automobile manufacturer uses the Internet to procure components and materials from vendors across the world. D) In an auction held on the Internet, a participant buys a product from another participant. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":91,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A single unit of Product A is composed of three (3) pieces of Part B and two (2) pieces of Part C. In the production plan for a particular period, when the demand for Product A is 10, which of the following is the net requirement of Part B? Here, the quantity in stock is five (5) for Part B, and there are no other pieces in stock, in process, on back order, or already allocated. The net requirement is calculated by subtracting the stock available for allocation from the gross requirement.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"25"},{"key":"C","text":"30"},{"key":"D","text":"45"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-39.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A single unit of Product A is composed of three (3) pieces of Part B and two (2) pieces of Part C. In the production plan for a particular period, when the demand for Product A is 10, which of the following is the net requirement of Part B? Here, the quantity in stock is five (5) for Part B, and there are no other pieces in stock, in process, on back order, or already allocated. The net requirement is calculated by subtracting the stock available for allocation from the gross requirement.” The correct answer is B) 25 because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 20 C) 30 D) 45 and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":92,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When the spreadsheet shown below is converted into CSV format, which of the following is an appropriate list of data that is generated by spreadsheet software? Here, records are separated by the carriage return code “CR”. The expression in a cell is automatically recalculated, and the resulting value is written back into that cell. Although the entered expressions are shown in row 3 and column C below, the resulting values are actually displayed on the screen.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"2 , 6 , 8 CR 7 , 4 , 11 CR 6 , 13 , 24 CR"},{"key":"B","text":"2 , 6 , 8 CR 7 , 4 , 11 CR 9 , 10 , 19 CR"},{"key":"C","text":"2 , 7 , 6 CR 6 , 4 , 13 CR 8 , 11 , 24 CR"},{"key":"D","text":"2 , 7 , 9 CR 6 , 4 , 10 CR 8 , 11 , 19 CR"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-40.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “When the spreadsheet shown below is converted into CSV format, which of the following is an appropriate list of data that is generated by spreadsheet software? Here, records are separated by the carriage return code “CR”. The expression in a cell is automatically recalculated, and the resulting value is written back into that cell. Although the entered expressions are shown in row 3 and column C below, the resulting values are actually displayed on the screen.” The correct answer is C) 2 , 7 , 6 CR 6 , 4 , 13 CR 8 , 11 , 24 CR because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) 2 , 6 , 8 CR 7 , 4 , 11 CR 6 , 13 , 24 CR B) 2 , 6 , 8 CR 7 , 4 , 11 CR 9 , 10 , 19 CR D) 2 , 7 , 9 CR 6 , 4 , 10 CR 8 , 11 , 19 CR and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":93,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate utilization of RPA for a company?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The adoption of an important strategy by management, such as an M&A"},{"key":"B","text":"The provision of a service that matches personal tastes"},{"key":"C","text":"The identification of patterns in large volumes of behavioral data concerning potential customers"},{"key":"D","text":"The streamlining of routine administrative work"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-40.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate utilization of RPA for a company?” The correct answer is D) The streamlining of routine administrative work because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) The adoption of an important strategy by management, such as an M&A B) The provision of a service that matches personal tastes C) The identification of patterns in large volumes of behavioral data concerning potential customers and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":94,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the analysis of big data?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In order to forecast unknown circumstances, analysis that uses machine learning in addition to statistical analysis is also effective."},{"key":"B","text":"Non-textual data in the form of video, images, and audio data cannot be in the scope of analysis."},{"key":"C","text":"Only information that spreads by humans, such as comments on an electronic bulletin board, social media messages, and website search history, is used in the analysis of human actions."},{"key":"D","text":"Data that is not intended to be analyzed, such as a blog entry, is out of the scope regardless of the purpose of analysis."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-41.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the analysis of big data?” The correct answer is A) In order to forecast unknown circumstances, analysis that uses machine learning in addition to statistical analysis is also effective. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Non-textual data in the form of video, images, and audio data cannot be in the scope of analysis. C) Only information that spreads by humans, such as comments on an electronic bulletin board, social media messages, and website search history, is used in the analysis of human actions. D) Data that is not intended to be analyzed, such as a blog entry, is out of the scope regardless of the purpose of analysis. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":95,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following analysis techniques used in Enterprise Architecture (EA) clarifies the issues by comparing the ideal situation with the current situation?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Gap analysis"},{"key":"B","text":"Core competence analysis"},{"key":"C","text":"Value chain analysis"},{"key":"D","text":"Pareto analysis"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-41.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following analysis techniques used in Enterprise Architecture (EA) clarifies the issues by comparing the ideal situation with the current situation?” The correct answer is A) Gap analysis because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Core competence analysis C) Value chain analysis D) Pareto analysis and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":96,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is “cloud computing”?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"One of the Internet communication protocols"},{"key":"B","text":"One of the service models for providing computer resources"},{"key":"C","text":"One of the software development methods for flexibly supporting changes in the specification"},{"key":"D","text":"One of the electronic data exchange standards for electronic commercial transactions"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-41.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is “cloud computing”?” The correct answer is B) One of the service models for providing computer resources because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) One of the Internet communication protocols C) One of the software development methods for flexibly supporting changes in the specification D) One of the electronic data exchange standards for electronic commercial transactions and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":97,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description of the Fourth Industrial Revolution?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The Internet and AI are utilized in a wide range of fields in daily life, such as medical care, infrastructure, and traffic systems, and service automation and quality improvement are achieved."},{"key":"B","text":"Production automation and labor cost reduction are achieved by the introduction to factories of industrial robots that utilize electronics."},{"key":"C","text":"Mass production of industrial products is performed by the construction of production lines that use conveyor belts in factories."},{"key":"D","text":"Productivity is increased compared to manual work by the use of steam energy as the driving force for machinery in light industry, such as sewing machines."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-42.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following is the most appropriate description of the Fourth Industrial Revolution?” The correct answer is A) The Internet and AI are utilized in a wide range of fields in daily life, such as medical care, infrastructure, and traffic systems, and service automation and quality improvement are achieved. because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are B) Production automation and labor cost reduction are achieved by the introduction to factories of industrial robots that utilize electronics. C) Mass production of industrial products is performed by the construction of production lines that use conveyor belts in factories. D) Productivity is increased compared to manual work by the use of steam energy as the driving force for machinery in light industry, such as sewing machines. and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":98,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"At power companies, the amount of electricity consumed by each household is measured remotely by communicating with electrical meters that are connected to the Internet, instead of measured by meter readings by a person. Which of the following is a term that represents the mechanism where a range of devices are connected to the Internet and utilize information in cases such as this?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"EDI"},{"key":"B","text":"IoT"},{"key":"C","text":"ISP"},{"key":"D","text":"RFID"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-42.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “At power companies, the amount of electricity consumed by each household is measured remotely by communicating with electrical meters that are connected to the Internet, instead of measured by meter readings by a person. Which of the following is a term that represents the mechanism where a range of devices are connected to the Internet and utilize information in cases such as this?” The correct answer is B) IoT because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) EDI C) ISP D) RFID and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":99,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following are international development targets that are composed of 17 objectives set by the United Nations in order to achieve a sustainable world?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"COP28"},{"key":"B","text":"SDGs"},{"key":"C","text":"UNESCO"},{"key":"D","text":"WHO"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-43.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “Which of the following are international development targets that are composed of 17 objectives set by the United Nations in order to achieve a sustainable world?” The correct answer is B) SDGs because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) COP28 C) UNESCO D) WHO and do not match the specific condition asked here."},{"id":100,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A company planning the development of a business information system decided to present an RFP to SIers. Which of the following must be described in the RFP at a minimum?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The development schedule"},{"key":"B","text":"The functions that should be implemented in the business information system"},{"key":"C","text":"The method for achieving the business information system"},{"key":"D","text":"The project team"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-43.png","explanation":"This question is testing the requirement described in the stem: “A company planning the development of a business information system decided to present an RFP to SIers. Which of the following must be described in the RFP at a minimum?” The correct answer is B) The functions that should be implemented in the business information system because it directly satisfies that requirement. The other choices are A) The development schedule C) The method for achieving the business information system D) The project team and do not match the specific condition asked here."}];